  "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"entry-content\"><div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><div class=\"vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid\"><div class=\"wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12\"><div class=\"vc_column-inner\"><div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n\t<div class=\"wpb_text_column wpb_content_element\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wpb_wrapper\">\n\t\t\t<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">To calculate your net carbs you subtract the following from the TOTAL CARBOHYDRATES:</span></p>\n<p align=\"center\"><strong><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Total Carbs&nbsp; –&nbsp; Fiber –&nbsp; Sugar Alcohols&nbsp;&nbsp; =&nbsp; Net&nbsp; Carbs</span></strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Using the label below, you would end up only counting 7 gm/net carbs after subtracting the fiber and sugar alcohols.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Just remember!&nbsp; SUGARS ALWAYS STAY IN THE COUNT, SO DON’T SUBTRACT THEM!</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_512\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-512\" style=\"width: 300px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https://journeylite.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/FoodLabel.png\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-512\" src=\"https://journeylite.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/FoodLabel-300x257.png\" alt=\"Food Label\" width=\"300\" height=\"257\" srcset=\"https://journeylite.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/FoodLabel-300x257.png 300w, https://journeylite.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/FoodLabel.png 349w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\"></a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-512\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Food Label</figcaption></figure>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n</div></div></div></div>\n</div></div>",
  "bodyMarkdown": "To calculate your net carbs you subtract the following from the TOTAL CARBOHYDRATES:\n\n**Total Carbs  –  Fiber –  Sugar Alcohols   =  Net  Carbs**\n\nUsing the label below, you would end up only counting 7 gm/net carbs after subtracting the fiber and sugar alcohols.\n\nJust remember!  SUGARS ALWAYS STAY IN THE COUNT, SO DON’T SUBTRACT THEM!\n\n<a href=\"https://journeylite.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/10/FoodLabel.png\"></a>Food Label",
